# Enforce LF in the repository and on checkout for every text file, on every
# platform, regardless of the developer's core.autocrlf / core.eol setting.
#
# Why this is load-bearing: a large share of the test suite asserts on the
# literal source text of components (e.g. `expect(ide).toContain('import {\n
# ...')`). On a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true those files land as
# CRLF and the `\n`-literal assertions fail locally while passing on the
# Linux CI runner — a confusing, recurring papercut. Pinning eol=lf makes a
# local checkout byte-identical to CI.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicit binary markers so a stray CRLF-normalisation pass can never corrupt
# these even if content auto-detection is ever fooled.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.webp  binary
*.zip   binary
*.gz    binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.wasm  binary
